Use io and string.

Define function valid_range taking text as a pointer to TcString, start as an unsigned number, span as an unsigned number returning a truth value:
    Let balance start at 0.
    For every i from start to start + span - 1:
        If text.data[i] equals 40:
            Add 1 to balance.
        Otherwise:
            Subtract 1 from balance.
            If balance is less than 0:
                Give back false.
    Give back balance equals 0.
Done.

Define function longest_valid taking text as a pointer to TcString returning a whole number:
    Let n be length of text.
    If n is 0:
        Give back 0.
    Let best start at 0 as an unsigned number.
    For every i from 0 as an unsigned number to n - 1:
        For every j from i to n - 1:
            Let span be j - i + 1.
            If span is more than best and valid_range(text, i, span):
                Set best to span.
    Give back best as a whole number.
Done.

Let first be str_from_bytes(bytes_ptr("(()"), bytes_len("(()")).
Let second be str_from_bytes(bytes_ptr(")()())"), bytes_len(")()())")).
Let third be str_from_bytes(bytes_ptr(""), bytes_len("")).
Say longest_valid(address of first).
Say longest_valid(address of second).
Say longest_valid(address of third).
str_free(address of first).
str_free(address of second).
str_free(address of third).
Return 0.
